  "body": "## Summary and dependency\n\nDraft, dependent on #371 (`codex/payphone-cancellation-compatibility-20260915`), after recovery worker #363 and the existing payment stack. Implements a strict-admin, read-only query-recovery operations report across backend/OpenAPI/web and matching generated mobile types. Mobile contract: https://github.com/diegueins680/TDF-mobile/pull/81 (head `d84fc3196202f2ac2468f78816b3c98fb4a22144`, draft, after mobile #79/#78/#64).\n\n- Add bounded `GET /admin/commerce/provider-queries`, default sandbox, with explicit schema availability, database flag, queue jobs and shared query budget timestamps.\n- Authorize before application validation/database access; read-only SQL and 3-second per-statement timeout; parameterized environment/status/pagination; fixed redacted 503; successful/503 responses use no-store.\n- Return only internal IDs, protocol states, counts/timestamps and a fixed diagnostic projection. No merchant/provider references, raw payloads, lease tokens or arbitrary stored errors.\n- Add responsive Spanish/English admin panel with stale/error/environment isolation, bounded paging and clear distinctions between completed query vs successful payment and enabled DB flag vs worker/merchant readiness.\n- No manual retry/reset, charge, refund, payout, provider activation, native admin screen, or new SQL migration.\n- Add security/contract/DB/UI tests, preserve catalog audit with two explicit technical-constant reviews, and document architecture, rollout and evidence.\n\n## Verified local tests (2026-09-15 UTC)\n\n- `cd tdf-hq && stack test --fast --rerun-tests`: **2,596 examples, 0 failures**, final run 24.4156 s, exit 0, observed 15:03:09.\n- `sh scripts/test-provider-retry-runtime.sh` with the documented isolated PostgreSQL 16.10 Unix-socket test URL: **133 examples, 0 failures**, 19.0567 s, complete harness exit 0 at 14:56:56. Includes parent migration repetition, empty rollback/flag preservation, populated rollback refusal/history checks, query timeout and read-only regressions. Provider I/O is mocked; this is not a provider sandbox test. Cluster stopped and exact-path status verified.\n- Five scoped web suites (panel/API/admin page/hosted checkout/provider return): **24 tests passed**, 64.418 s. After lint found two test promises, fixed async/await and reran scoped ESLint with zero warnings plus both API tests successfully. No rule disabled.\n- Web/mobile typecheck passed; both clients generated with openapi-typescript 7.10.1 and byte-identical. Mobile initial missing dependencies were repaired with locked npm ci; no manifest/lock changes.\n- `npm run quality:repo`: passed, including 157 Node tests across nine groups, formal audit and generated-artifact drift guard.\n- Final catalog/contract Node run: **5 tests passed**. Final tracked-source `--fail-on-unreviewed` audit: **1,422 files / 1,128 candidates, 0 unreviewed / 0 stale**, generated 15:04:36.948. Existing entries/gates preserved.\n- `git diff --check` and local documentation links passed.\n\nRuntime commits: `a1a6350f852a01eb6134ccb8ae742e5a9b12ac9f` (backend/API), `9fddf58037c1780402fe5393d1d4694e005d765e` (web/clients), `0ffe9d666debb12bc5492fb978e951b9dd5988a0` (test promises). Later changes are review/evidence docs only. Exact commands, observations and baseline failures: `docs/payments/query-observability-2026-09-15.md`. Architecture: ADR 0122. Parent CI was still running its backend check at last inspection; no new-PR CI success is claimed here.\n\n## How to exercise after authorized staging qualification\n\nBuild/test the API with Stack only (`cd tdf-hq && stack test --fast --rerun-tests`), generate clients using `npm run generate:api`, then deploy reviewed backend before web using the existing approved workflow. No deployment was performed in this increment.\n\nIllustrative curl only (not executed; placeholders are not credentials):\n\n```sh\ncurl --fail-with-body \\\n  -H 'Authorization: Bearer <approved-strict-admin-session-token>' \\\n  'https://<authorized-api>/admin/commerce/provider-queries?environment=sandbox&status=dead_letter&limit=25&offset=0'\n```\n\nUse the approved session/secret mechanism, not a real token pasted into source, logs or shell history. Inspect sandbox report freshness and compare original operation outcome separately from job state. Missing schema/404/failed request is unavailable evidence, not an empty queue. The report does not include unknown-resource operations that cannot enter the bound-resource worker queue.\n\n## Migration, rollback and integration cautions\n\nNo new migration/backfill; parent SQL and checksums untouched. Roll back endpoint/panel without deleting or resetting any historical job. Parent worker/provider qualification gates remain unchanged. Offset pages are a live operational view, not a stable financial export; production-sized latency is untested.\n\nLatest root main advanced during work to `52b32e4c17b3b0485c66e666137f85d44cc962d4` (#369 artwork). Its unrelated six-file change was inspected; catalog-review entries overlap. Preserve both sets and rerun the gate when updating the parent stack; this dependent diff deliberately contains no unrelated artwork implementation.\n\nMobile payment lineage diverges from latest main `d4a1b17c733f57f912d36e7e396f6869cfd18c8a`; do not replace the gitlink with bare main and lose pending payment/RSVP work. Separately reviewed mobile #80 social schema also needs combined-schema regeneration after merge. No reconciliation of those mobile lineages is claimed.\n\n## Blocked and unexecuted\n\nStaging read-only inspector at 14:22:31.992 found healthy public API/web endpoints, but six hosting checks returned `hosting_authentication_unavailable`; deployed source SHA unknown, providerQualified=false. Restore approved app-scoped `FLY_STAGING_API_TOKEN` / `FLY_STAGING_WEB_TOKEN` or authorized local Fly login, then verify sandbox account/contract/webhook readiness. No secret values read or printed.\n\nNo credentialed provider sandbox/E2E, authenticated staging report, native device/Expo runtime, screenshots, production-size load, production deployment or live transaction was performed. This draft is not a formal native-runtime review request. Unknown-resource/manual recovery, remaining provider/business flows and compliant marketplace payouts remain unfinished; legal/accounting/PCI decisions still require qualified review. No claim of whole-platform completion or certification. Keep draft and unmerged.\n",
